# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.r39quiet).
#
# R39, the GLES-only lockscreen round: the boot path NEVER puts the Metal discovery
# properties on the IOAcceleratorES service.  Structural, not temporal -- R38's device log
# (4803 lines, read in full) killed the containment idea for good:
#
#   - R37's own verdict stands (J1 SENTINEL ESTABLISHED, the r38 release body records it):
#     inside the props window the chain completed -- RedwoodGPU client opened (0),
#     MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice() = "Adreno 7c+ Gen 3 (chip 0x6040001, Redwood)", class
#     RedwoodMetalDevice, the 11-class 420+-method sweep answered.  The discovery chain and
#     our RedwoodGPU user client are ALIVE.
#
#   - But R38 proved the window itself is a lottery: analyticsd walked first and died at
#     the frontier (signal 10 at 0x1e32e491c seconds after metal_props on, before
#     metal_test's own crash), and after that first frontier death EVERY process born
#     afterwards died in dyld -- lsd respawned 78 times to the end of the log INCLUDING
#     with the properties already OFF (spawned 00:03:43.036, dead 00:03:43.057 -- 21 ms),
#     analyticsd x4, mobilegestalt.xpc, and backboardd itself at 00:04:56 on the first
#     touch ("signal 10 at 0x1e32e491c, pc 0x18dcd091c" right after the event server asked
#     for AccurateMaxDigitizerPressureValue).  R36 saw the same shape (mobilegestalt.xpc
#     died BEFORE metal_test; backboardd x9).  One frontier death poisons the boot for
#     every page-in that follows; whether the walker survives (R37) or dies (R36/R38) is
#     not ours to choose.  The white Apple = CA's boot backdrop frozen at frame 4 / flip 3
#     because mobilegestalt.xpc and lsd -- SpringBoard's own dependencies -- were the
#     plague's casualties.
#
#   - The reference reached the same conclusion from the other side: docs/RAPHAEL.md
#     2026-10-27, "upstream has merged the userland, removed Metal" -- GLES-only, and their
#     phone-proven lockscreen/UI/GPU round (2026-10-23) ran backboardd on "the project's
#     existing GLES CoreAnimation path" all along.  Our GLES road is the same and is
#     ALREADY PROVEN on the device: R38's log has redwood-gl frames 1..4 finishing cleanly
#     (finish_update -> 0) and the kernel display latching flips 1..3 -- the whole
#     compositor pipeline works; it was starved, not broken.
#
# So this list is the pre-Metal probe set VERBATIM (the base rc.jobs, R34-lineage, last
# ridden by a shipped volume before the metal rounds), and NOTHING of the discovery chain
# runs: no metal_props, no metal_test, no sweep.  Metal's J1 verdict is already on the
# record from R37; re-measuring it costs a poisoned boot.  The WiFi half of R39 rides the
# kernel's wifi=1 (the raphael branch needs no daemon and dies quietly when the modem
# firmware is absent from the RAM image -- this volume carries none).
#
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn started by launchd
/redwood/bin/svc_test
/redwood/bin/surf_test
/bin/ps -A
/redwood/bin/mg_test
# the processors: how many, and -- once the system has settled -- whether they work at the same time
/redwood/bin/cpu_test
/redwood/bin/cpu_test 240 &
